{
  "id": "partition-list",
  "questionId": "partition-list",
  "slug": "partition-list",
  "title": "Partition List",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Fast slow pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "fast & slow pointers",
    "linked list",
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you need two groups that each preserve their original relative order - what if you built each group as its own small list while walking the original once?",
    "keep two separate 'tail' pointers, one for the less-than-x chain being built and one for the greater-or-equal chain",
    "walk through the original list once; for each node, append it to the appropriate chain's tail depending on its value versus x",
    "once you've processed every node, link the tail of the less-than chain to the head of the greater-or-equal chain to join them, and make sure the final tail's next is terminated"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using strictly greater than x instead of greater-or-equal when deciding which partition a value belongs to",
    "forgetting to terminate the merged list's tail, leaving a stray connection if reusing original node references",
    "not preserving relative order within a partition (e.g. accidentally reversing one of the two chains while building it)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A singly linked list is given to you as an array `nums`, where `nums[i]` is\nthe value of the i-th node in order, along with an integer `x`.\n\n**Rearrange the list so that all nodes with a value less than `x` come before all nodes with a value greater than or equal to `x`, and return the resulting list's values in order.**\n\nThe relative order of nodes within each of the two groups must be preserved.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 200",
      "-100 <= nums[i] <= 100",
      "-200 <= x <= 200"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an empty list",
      "all values already less than x, or all values already >= x",
      "x smaller than every value or larger than every value"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 2], x = 3",
        "output": "[1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]",
        "explanation": "values less than 3, in order: 1,2,2; values >= 3, in order: 4,3,5"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [2, 1], x = 2",
        "output": "[1, 2]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2]",
        "explanation": "1 < 2 comes first, then 2 >= 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3], x = 10",
        "output": "[1, 2, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 3]",
        "explanation": "every value is less than x, so order is unchanged"
      }
    ],
